    <h2>What we install</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Smart switches and dimmers, including in boxes that never had a neutral.</li>
        <li>Video doorbells with properly sized transformers.</li>
        <li>Security cameras with power where you want them.</li>
        <li>Ethernet to the rooms that need it, and ceiling-mounted Wi-Fi access points.</li>
        <li>Whole-home surge protection at the panel, which protects all of the above.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Wired where it counts</h2>
    <p>Wi-Fi is convenient; a cable is reliable. A run to the home office, the TV and each access point takes most of the strain off your wireless network, and is far cheaper to add during other electrical work.</p>
